        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory business audience.",
          "text": "An information system is not just an application. Imagine a customer places an order. A person confirms the request, a process defines what should happen next, data records the facts, and technology moves that record to the people who fulfill and monitor the order. A useful system coordinates all four parts around a business outcome."
        },
